{"id":"afef6bcc-df28-45af-a274-a3c0c8544730","expr":"b == 0 ? result == Integer.MIN_VALUE : result == a / b","rationale":"Captures the method's documented behavior: if b is 0, returns MIN_VALUE, else returns integer division.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:06.607037Z"}
{"id":"b32b1fa0-e9b9-4f95-a6b5-58b8b6e353ee","expr":"b == 0 || a / b * b + a % b == a","rationale":"If b == 0, division is not performed; otherwise, basic property of integer division and modulus ensures this holds.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:06.607147Z"}
{"id":"d73ba48a-8e66-45f6-90df-51e53c2b9170","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The 'args' parameter, supplied by the JVM to main, is never null in standard usage.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:06.607212Z"}
{"id":"7650a3c5-90a8-49e7-92d2-9aac13d19807","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The 'args' parameter should be non-null during execution of 'main' as per Java runtime guarantees.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:06.607112Z"}
{"id":"61e4ed4f-faef-4ef6-b71f-a06cf12fec69","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"All arrays in Java have a non-negative length.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:06.607212Z"}
{"id":"f0028011-bf33-4e81-9ca6-a434e9adf037","expr":"b != 0 || Integer.MIN_VALUE == Integer.MIN_VALUE","rationale":"If b is 0, the method returns Integer.MIN_VALUE, so this invariant is trivially always true but conveys method's documented behavior.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:06.607147Z"}
{"id":"84bc2a6e-34bb-4a27-ab59-8e080a60edf0","expr":"b == 0 || result == a / b","rationale":"If b is not zero, result is exactly a / b.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:06.607037Z"}
{"id":"a25b7536-b6c5-4bfa-9bf2-46073851082a","expr":"(b > 0) || (b <= 0)","rationale":"This covers all integer possibilities for b, and is useful as a partitioning fact.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:06.607147Z"}
{"id":"9d671061-e024-425b-966e-37e378602a36","expr":"args.getClass().isArray()","rationale":"The 'args' variable is always a Java array.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:06.607212Z"}
{"id":"808399ec-4dd1-487c-8604-ca083de97547","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"The length of an array in Java is always non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:06.607112Z"}
{"id":"5b1715f2-0ed0-413f-a9a6-036a86a76903","expr":"a == 0 || a != 0","rationale":"This partitions the input space regarding 'a'; while tautological, it helps coverage analysis.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:06.607147Z"}
{"id":"ec14ecc4-ada0-40a1-96dc-e71161f8cce9","expr":"b == 0 || b * result <= a && a < b * (result + 1)","rationale":"If b != 0, result is integer division so this gives the mathematical bounds for a in integer division.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:06.607037Z"}
{"id":"f54ebc98-9953-4896-8473-977667bf9b0c","expr":"b != 0 || result == Integer.MIN_VALUE","rationale":"If b is zero, result must be Integer.MIN_VALUE.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:06.607037Z"}
{"id":"43e75464-040f-4f89-9fb0-28c6bfdfe831","expr":"b == 0 || Math.abs(result) <= Math.abs(a)","rationale":"If b != 0, division reduces the magnitude or keeps it the same.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:00:06.607037Z"}
